{"entryId":"1433","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1433:1","sourceSha256":"a94db6187633d7a37ee19965c9f650fd959f953db5251c41c2ffaaa92038a26b","englishSha256":"8725531cdf10e87507b660a14b40b7d2580088881ad3a16d346d835a2cf7d978","citations":[{"id":"1433:1:citation-01","he":[0,30],"en":[20,29],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Taanit_7a.15"},"reference":"Taanit 7a:15","assessment":"The exact Bavli names Rabbi Chanina bar Idi comparing Torah to water.","evidence":[{"reference":"Taanit 7a:15","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Taanit_7a.15"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1433:1:citation-02","he":[32,117],"en":[31,44],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Moed_Katan_5a.20"},"reference":"Moed Katan 5a:20","assessment":"The Bavli omits Chinena’s patronymic and names Yehoshua son of Rav Idi separately. The anthology marks the first patronymic in parentheses and gives Hoshea in the second position.","evidence":[{"reference":"Moed Katan 5a:20","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Moed_Katan_5a.20"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Ein Yaakov, Moed Katan 1:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ein_Yaakov%2C_Moed_Katan_1.1"},"witness":"Daat"}]},{"id":"1433:1:citation-03","he":[32,117],"en":[77,93],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ein_Yaakov%2C_Moed_Katan_1.1"},"reference":"Ein Yaakov, Moed Katan 1:1","assessment":"The Bavli omits Chinena’s patronymic and names Yehoshua son of Rav Idi separately. The anthology marks the first patronymic in parentheses and gives Hoshea in the second position.","evidence":[{"reference":"Moed Katan 5a:20","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Moed_Katan_5a.20"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Ein Yaakov, Moed Katan 1:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ein_Yaakov%2C_Moed_Katan_1.1"},"witness":"Daat"}]},{"id":"1433:1:citation-04","he":[119,212],"en":[277,289],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Pesachim_75a.3"},"reference":"Pesachim 75a:3","assessment":"The exact two segments distinguish Chinena bar Idi questioning Adda and Chinena the Elder transmitting Assi and Yochanan.","evidence":[{"reference":"Pesachim 75a:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Pesachim_75a.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Pesachim 75a:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Pesachim_75a.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1433:1:citation-05","he":[214,348],"en":[291,324],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Avodah_Zarah_40a.9"},"reference":"Avodah Zarah 40a:9","assessment":"The full Avodah Zarah supplies jars as the contents of the trough and the fish in one of them. The exact source gives the three named authorities without a studenthood conclusion.","evidence":[{"reference":"Avodah Zarah 40a:9","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Avodah_Zarah_40a.9"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1433:1:citation-06","he":[349,407],"en":[553,567],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Avodah_Zarah_40a.9.3"},"reference":"Rashi on Avodah Zarah 40a:9:3","assessment":"The exact Rashi explains the metaphor of the three Scriptures as three sages with authority comparable to Scripture.","evidence":[{"reference":"Rashi on Avodah Zarah 40a:9:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Avodah_Zarah_40a.9.3"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"1433:1:citation-07","he":[570,616],"en":[879,924],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mekhilta_DeRabbi_Yishmael%2C_Tractate_Amalek_2.15"},"reference":"Mekhilta DeRabbi Yishmael, Tractate Amalek 2:15","assessment":"The exact Mekhilta reads Chananyah ben Adi in the Moses tradition. The received Idi form and identity question remain.","evidence":[{"reference":"Mekhilta DeRabbi Yishmael, Tractate Amalek 2:15","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mekhilta_DeRabbi_Yishmael%2C_Tractate_Amalek_2.15"},"witness":"Beeri Edition, Koren, Jerusalem, 2019"}]},{"id":"1433:1:citation-08","he":[618,671],"en":[949,969],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mekhilta_DeRabbi_Yishmael%2C_Tractate_Nezikin_5.30"},"reference":"Mekhilta DeRabbi Yishmael, Tractate Nezikin 5:30","assessment":"The exact Mekhilta gives Chananyah ben Adi in the oath discussion, with a received Chanina ben Idi variant in Heilprin.","evidence":[{"reference":"Mekhilta DeRabbi Yishmael, Tractate Nezikin 5:30","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mekhilta_DeRabbi_Yishmael%2C_Tractate_Nezikin_5.30"},"witness":"Beeri Edition, Koren, Jerusalem, 2019"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,3,4,5,6,7],"holds":[{"raw":"אולי אחיו הוא","reason":"The inference is tentative. The Bavli has only bare Chinena in the first clause, and the anthology adds a parenthetic patronymic while giving Hoshea in the second.","evidence":[{"reference":"Moed Katan 5a:20","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Moed_Katan_5a.20"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Ein Yaakov, Moed Katan 1:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ein_Yaakov%2C_Moed_Katan_1.1"},"witness":"Daat"}]},{"raw":"והיוחסין הביא גם ר' חנינא בר אידי והכל אחד הוא","reason":"The exact Yuchasin listing remains unlocated. Keep the identification attributed.","evidence":[]},{"raw":"תלמיד שמואל. לא ידעתי מנ\"ל","reason":"The three named authorities occur in the dialogue, and the narrator explicitly questions the student label.","evidence":[{"reference":"Avodah Zarah 40a:9","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Avodah_Zarah_40a.9"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"ומסופק אני אם זה הוא","reason":"The two Mekhilta passages give Chananyah ben Adi. Preserve the compiler’s explicit uncertainty about identity.","evidence":[{"reference":"Mekhilta DeRabbi Yishmael, Tractate Amalek 2:15","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mekhilta_DeRabbi_Yishmael%2C_Tractate_Amalek_2.15"},"witness":"Beeri Editio